WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:13.290
Hi! Prepositions are small words like at, on and in, but using the wrong one changes the meaning. Today we'll learn prepositions of time, place and some fixed phrases.

2
00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:19.554
For time, use at for a clock time, like at 7 o'clock. We also say at night.

3
00:00:19.704 --> 00:00:24.018
Use on for days and dates, like on Monday and on 5 June.

4
00:00:24.168 --> 00:00:31.554
Use in for months, years and parts of the day, like in June, in 2026 and in the morning.

5
00:00:31.704 --> 00:00:35.874
For place, use in for inside something, like in the box.

6
00:00:36.024 --> 00:00:40.554
Use on for on top of a surface, like on the box or on the table.

7
00:00:40.704 --> 00:00:44.418
Use next to or beside for something at the side.

8
00:00:44.568 --> 00:00:54.114
For movement, across means from one side to the other, like walk across the road. Through means passing inside, like through the tunnel.

9
00:00:54.264 --> 00:01:01.914
Some prepositions always go with certain words, so learn them as a set: good at, afraid of, interested in.

10
00:01:02.064 --> 00:01:05.610
Also proud of, different from and depend on.

11
00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:09.402
Congratulate someone on, and look forward to.

12
00:01:09.552 --> 00:01:12.714
For example: She is good at maths.

13
00:01:12.864 --> 00:01:16.506
He is afraid of spiders.

14
00:01:16.656 --> 00:01:20.562
Watch out! He is good in swimming is wrong!

15
00:01:20.712 --> 00:01:24.906
The fixed phrase is good at, so we say He is good at swimming.

16
00:01:25.056 --> 00:01:30.738
Learn fixed phrases as a whole, and never swap the preposition.

17
00:01:30.888 --> 00:01:40.890
Your turn! We have a spelling test ___ Friday. Which preposition? Pause and think.

18
00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:47.250
The answer is on, because we use on with days. Did you get it right?

19
00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:58.050
Another one! The cat ran ___ the road, from one side to the other. What goes in? Pause and think.

20
00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:03.210
The answer is across. Did you get it right?

21
00:02:03.360 --> 00:02:13.458
Try this one! We are having a party ___ Friday. Which preposition? Pause and think.

22
00:02:13.608 --> 00:02:20.658
The answer is on. We use on before days of the week. Did you get it right?

23
00:02:20.808 --> 00:02:30.858
And another! I usually read a book ___ night. Which preposition? Pause and think.

24
00:02:31.008 --> 00:02:37.914
The answer is at. We say in the morning, but at night. Did you get it right?

25
00:02:38.064 --> 00:02:48.474
Last one! My brother is interested ___ insects. What's the preposition? Pause and think.

26
00:02:48.624 --> 00:02:55.530
The answer is in. Interested in is a fixed phrase. Did you get it right?

27
00:02:55.680 --> 00:03:08.370
Remember: at for clock times, on for days and dates, in for months and years. In means inside, on means on a surface, and across means from one side to the other. Learn fixed phrases as a whole.

28
00:03:08.520 --> 00:03:12.522
Make a sentence with good at today!

